---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import OperationsPreview from '../components/OperationsPreview.astro';
import release from '../data/release.json';
---
<Marketing>
 <section class="hero"><div class="container">
  <a href="/releases/" class="release-pill"><b>v{release.version}</b><span>Explore the current preview</span><Icon name="arrow" size={12}/></a>
  <div class="hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted service desk</p><h1>Your service desk.<br/>Under <span class="gradient-text">your control.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">Incidents, email and service requests in one place. Connect your helpdesk to automation and AI, with your infrastructure and access rules.</p><div class="hero-ctas"><a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/" class="button">Deploy RatelDesk <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a><a href="/docs/" class="button button-secondary"><Icon name="book" size={15}/>Explore the docs</a></div><p class="hero-footnote"><Icon name="check" size={12}/>Open source · Self-hosted · AI optional</p></div><OperationsPreview/></div>
 </div></section>
 <div class="platform-strip"><div class="container"><span class="strip-label">A connected support workflow</span><span class="platform-item"><Icon name="mail" size={16}/>Email <small>Microsoft 365 · IMAP · POP3</small></span><span class="platform-item"><Icon name="flow" size={16}/>Self-service <small>NetRatel automation</small></span><span class="platform-item"><Icon name="spark" size={16}/>AI assistants <small>Netclaw · MCP</small></span></div></div>
 <section class="section" id="platform"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">The service workspace</p><h2>Make the next step<br/>obvious.</h2></div><p>Keep the request, the conversation and the work together. Give your team the context to move things forward.</p></div>
  <div class="capability-grid">
   <article class="capability"><div class="capability-icon"><Icon name="inbox" size={22}/></div><h3>Keep support connected.</h3><p>Bring incoming mail into your helpdesk. Work through incidents, public replies and internal notes, with organization context close at hand.</p><div class="capability-chips"><span>Incidents</span><span>Email</span><span>Worklogs</span></div><a href="/docs/guides/incidents/" class="text-link">Work through an incident <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></a><div class="mail-mini" aria-hidden="true"><span><i></i>Message received</span><span><i></i>Ticket updated</span><span><i></i>Reply submitted</span></div></article>
   <article class="capability"><div class="capability-icon"><Icon name="flow" size={22}/></div><h3>Make self-service useful.</h3><p>Build request forms that collect the right details. Map their inputs to a configured NetRatel job and follow the execution from the request.</p><div class="inline-points"><span><Icon name="check" size={12}/>Forms for your services</span><span><Icon name="check" size={12}/>Explicit job and input mappings</span><span><Icon name="check" size={12}/>Run status and results</span></div><a href="/docs/automation/self-service-forms/" class="text-link">Build a self-service request <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></a></article>
   <article class="capability"><div class="capability-icon"><Icon name="spark" size={22}/></div><h3>Bring AI into the work.</h3><p>Use Netclaw for ticket conversations. Give external assistants a defined role through MCP, with permissions tied to their configured access.</p><div class="mini-terminal"><span>Ticket chat</span> → Connected Netclaw<br/><span>Assistant tools</span> → RatelDesk MCP<br/><span>Your access rules</span> → Every operation</div><a href="/docs/integrations/netclaw/" class="text-link">Explore AI connections <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></a></article>
  </div>
 </div></section>
 <section class="section workflow-section" id="automation"><div class="container workflow-grid"><div class="workflow-copy"><p class="eyebrow">RatelDesk + NetRatel</p><h2>From a request<br/>to a finished job.</h2><p>A request form can be the front door to your automation. Collect the details in RatelDesk, map them to a reviewed NetRatel job, and follow its progress.</p><p>Your helpdesk owns the service request. Your orchestrator runs the configured work. The connection keeps them together.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/automation/job-bindings/">Connect forms to automation <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a><div class="paired-note"><Icon name="activity" size={18}/><p>It works in the other direction too: turn a NetRatel monitoring alert into a RatelDesk incident. <a href="/docs/integrations/netratel/">See the integration →</a></p></div></div>
 <div class="workflow-visual" role="img" aria-label="Example self-service flow: a requester submits a RatelDesk form, its inputs map to a configured NetRatel job, and the run status is available from the linked request."><div class="workflow-title"><span>Example self-service workflow</span><Icon name="flow" size={15}/></div><div class="request-preview"><div class="request-preview-title"><Icon name="layers" size={19}/>Create a team workspace</div><div><span>Team</span><strong>Research</strong></div><div><span>Workspace name</span><strong>Project Atlas</strong></div><p>Details collected by your request form</p></div><div class="flow-connector"></div><div class="flow-node">NetRatel · Configured job + inputs</div><div class="flow-connector"></div><div class="workflow-result"><Icon name="check" size={17}/><div>Follow the result<small>Run status linked to the RatelDesk request</small></div></div><p class="flow-legend">Define the job. Review the mapping. Make the service available.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="section teams-section"><div class="container integrations-intro"><div class="integrations-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Meet people where they work</p><h2>Your helpdesk assistant.<br/>In Microsoft Teams.</h2><p>Connect a Teams-enabled Netclaw deployment to RatelDesk through MCP. Let people ask questions and work with the helpdesk data and actions their configured identity can access.</p><p>The guide covers the Teams connection, the RatelDesk credential and a first permitted read.</p><a href="/docs/integrations/microsoft-teams/" class="text-link">Set up Teams + Netclaw <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a></div><div class="teams-preview"><div class="teams-preview-head"><span class="teams-symbol" aria-hidden="true">T</span><div><strong>Helpdesk assistant</strong><span>Microsoft Teams + Netclaw</span></div><span class="example-badge">Example</span></div><div class="teams-message user"><span>You</span>Can you summarise the open incidents I can access?</div><div class="teams-message assistant"><span><Icon name="spark" size={12}/>Helpdesk assistant</span>I can check RatelDesk and bring back the current status, owner and next step for each incident.<div class="tool-chip"><Icon name="lock" size={11}/>RatelDesk MCP · Permitted access</div></div><p>Illustrative conversation · Requires a Teams-enabled Netclaw deployment</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="section integrations-section" id="integrations"><div class="container"><div class="integrations-intro"><div class="integrations-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Connected by design</p><h2>One helpdesk.<br/>More ways to work.</h2><p>Use the browser, your terminal or an assistant. Connect mail and automation through explicit configurations, with access you can review.</p><a href="/docs/integrations/overview/" class="text-link">Find your integration path <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a></div><div class="integration-list"><a class="integration-tile" href="/docs/integrations/http-mcp/"><Icon name="globe" size={23}/><div><h3>HTTP MCP</h3><p>Remote assistant access</p></div><span>↗</span></a><a class="integration-tile" href="/docs/integrations/stdio/"><Icon name="terminal" size={23}/><div><h3>stdio MCP</h3><p>Local assistant tooling</p></div><span>↗</span></a><a class="integration-tile" href="/docs/reference/cli/"><Icon name="code" size={23}/><div><h3>RatelDesk CLI</h3><p>Your command-line workflow</p></div><span>↗</span></a><a class="integration-tile" href="/docs/email/overview/"><Icon name="mail" size={23}/><div><h3>Email</h3><p>Mailboxes, routing & replies</p></div><span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="auth-strip"><div><Icon name="shield" size={23}/><div>Sign in the way your team works.<p>Local accounts, OpenID Connect through Authentik, or both.</p></div></div><div class="auth-links"><a href="/docs/identity/local/">Local</a><a href="/docs/identity/oidc/">OIDC</a><a href="/docs/identity/hybrid/">Hybrid</a></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="section start-section" id="get-started"><div class="container start-grid"><div class="start-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h2>A clear path<br/>to your first request.</h2><p>Deploy your helpdesk. Connect a mailbox. Add the tools you need.</p><div class="start-options" role="tablist" aria-label="Getting started paths"><button role="tab" id="start-tab-server" aria-controls="start-server" aria-selected="true" data-start="server"><Icon name="server" size={18}/>Deploy RatelDesk<Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></button><button role="tab" id="start-tab-email" aria-controls="start-email" aria-selected="false" data-start="email" tabindex="-1"><Icon name="mail" size={18}/>Connect email<Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></button><button role="tab" id="start-tab-mcp" aria-controls="start-mcp" aria-selected="false" data-start="mcp" tabindex="-1"><Icon name="spark" size={18}/>Connect an assistant<Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></button></div></div><div>
  <div class="start-panel" id="start-server" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="start-tab-server" tabindex="0"><div class="start-panel-head"><span>01 / SERVER</span><span>Docker Compose · Self-hosted</span></div><div class="start-panel-body"><h3>Start with the release bundle.</h3><p>Download the deployment files, verify the checksum and follow the first-run setup. These guides target the current v{release.version} preview.</p><div class="command"><code id="download-command">curl -fLO https://github.com/BostonTechnologies/rateldesk/releases/download/{release.tag}/rateldesk-deployment-{release.version}.tar.gz</code><button class="copy-command" data-copy="download-command" aria-label="Copy download command"><Icon name="copy" size={15}/></button></div><p class="start-note">Choose your storage, configure the instance and create the first administrator.</p><a href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/" class="text-link">Follow the deployment guide <Icon name="arrow" size={14}/></a></div></div>
  <div class="start-panel" id="start-email" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="start-tab-email" tabindex="0" hidden><div class="start-panel-head"><span>02 / EMAIL</span><span>Microsoft 365 · IMAP · POP3</span></div><div class="start-panel-body"><h3>Bring the support mailbox with you.</h3><p>Choose a mailbox connection and its organization routing. Configure incoming and outgoing mail, then follow a test message through the helpdesk.</p><div class="mini-terminal"><span>1.</span> Connect the mailbox<br/><span>2.</span> Review routing and delivery settings<br/><span>3.</span> Test a new message and a reply</div><p class="start-note">The mail guides cover authentication, threading, imports and delivery history.</p><a href="/docs/email/overview/" class="text-link">Set up email support <Icon name="arrow" size={14}/></a></div></div>
  <div class="start-panel" id="start-mcp" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="start-tab-mcp" tabindex="0" hidden><div class="start-panel-head"><span>03 / ASSISTANT</span><span>Scoped tools · Explicit access</span></div><div class="start-panel-body"><h3>Give your assistant a defined role.</h3><p>Choose remote HTTP MCP or a local stdio connection. Use the correct credential purpose and bind access to the intended organization and account.</p><div class="mini-terminal"><span>HTTP</span> Assistant → RatelDesk MCP → API<br/><span>stdio</span> Assistant → local process → API</div><p class="start-note">Start with authentication and a permitted read before using actions.</p><a href="/docs/integrations/overview/" class="text-link">Choose an assistant connection <Icon name="arrow" size={14}/></a></div></div>
 </div></div></section>
 <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Documentation that gets to the point</p><h2>Find the next thing you need.</h2></div><a href="/docs/" class="text-link">Browse all documentation <Icon name="arrow" size={14}/></a></div><div class="doc-paths"><a class="doc-path" href="/docs/deployment/overview/"><span>01 / DEPLOY</span><h3>Run it your way.</h3><p>Compose, storage, HTTPS, backups and upgrades. Choose the setup that fits your environment.</p><span class="text-link">Deployment scenarios <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></span></a><a class="doc-path" href="/docs/automation/self-service-forms/"><span>02 / AUTOMATE</span><h3>Make requests actionable.</h3><p>Build service forms and connect them to the right NetRatel job, with useful inputs and visible results.</p><span class="text-link">Self-service automation <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></span></a><a class="doc-path" href="/docs/reference/architecture/"><span>03 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>See how it fits together.</h3><p>Understand the architecture, identity model and integration boundaries before extending your setup.</p><span class="text-link">Architecture & reference <Icon name="arrow" size={13}/></span></a></div></div></section>
 <section class="cta-section"><div class="container cta-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow">Built by Boston Technologies</p><h2>Own your service desk.</h2><p>Deploy RatelDesk. Connect your team. Give every request a clear next step.</p><div class="cta-actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart/">Get started <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/BostonTechnologies/rateldesk">View on GitHub <Icon name="arrowUp" size={14}/></a></div></div><img class="cta-art" src="/brand/rateldesk-mark-512.webp" width="512" height="512" alt="RatelDesk honey badger mascot" loading="lazy"/></div></section>
</Marketing>
<script>
 const tabs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-start]'));
 function activate(tab: HTMLButtonElement) { for(const t of tabs){ const selected=t===tab;t.setAttribute('aria-selected',String(selected));t.tabIndex=selected?0:-1;const pane=document.getElementById(`start-${t.dataset.start}`);if(pane)pane.hidden=!selected;} }
 tabs.forEach((tab,i)=>{tab.addEventListener('click',()=>activate(tab));tab.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(['ArrowRight','ArrowLeft','ArrowDown','ArrowUp','Home','End'].includes(e.key)){e.preventDefault();const index=e.key==='Home'?0:e.key==='End'?tabs.length-1:(i+(['ArrowRight','ArrowDown'].includes(e.key)?1:-1)+tabs.length)%tabs.length;activate(tabs[index]);tabs[index].focus();}});});
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', async()=>{const code=document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy||'')?.textContent;if(!code)return;try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code);button.setAttribute('aria-label','Command copied');button.innerHTML='<span style="font-size:10px">Copied</span>';setTimeout(()=>{button.setAttribute('aria-label','Copy download command');button.innerHTML='<span style="font-size:10px">Copy</span>';},1800);}catch{const selection=window.getSelection();const range=document.createRange();const source=document.getElementById(button.dataset.copy||'');if(source){range.selectNodeContents(source);selection?.removeAllRanges();selection?.addRange(range);button.setAttribute('aria-label','Select and copy the command');}}}));
</script>
